#!/usr/local/bin/dyalogscript
⍝ Phase 8 (ADR D17): the same generalization as test/12, applied
⍝ identically to JsonRpcCl (Content-Length framing) — pipelined
⍝ Send/AwaitResponse with out-of-order arrival, CallBatch, and
⍝ notification dispatch (registered handler vs. backward-compatible
⍝ fallthrough to h.Notifications). No Mcp-level test here — Mcp is
⍝ built on JsonRpc, not JsonRpcCl (see README's Layer diagram).
⎕IO←1
⎕FIX'file://D:/devel/mcp-client/src/JsonRpcCl.dyalog'

h←JsonRpcCl.Connect'python' 'D:\devel\mcp-client\examples\toy-jsonrpc-cl-pipeline-server.py'
h.Timeout←10

⍝ --- Pipelined Send/AwaitResponse: out-of-order arrival ---
t0←⎕AI[3]
slowId←h JsonRpcCl.Send('delay'(seconds:2 ⋄ text:'slow'))
fastId←h JsonRpcCl.Send('echo'(text:'fast'))
fastResp←h JsonRpcCl.AwaitResponse fastId
fastElapsed←⎕AI[3]-t0
⎕←'fast response -> ',fastResp.result,' (',(⍕fastElapsed),'ms after send)'
⎕←'fast arrived well before slow''s 2000ms delay: ',⍕fastElapsed<1500

slowResp←h JsonRpcCl.AwaitResponse slowId
⎕←'slow response -> ',slowResp.result

⍝ Call is unchanged: Send then immediately AwaitResponse on that id.
r←h JsonRpcCl.Call('echo'(text:'plain call'))
⎕←'plain call -> ',r.result

⍝ --- CallBatch: same reversed-reply-order proof as test/12 ---
batchArgs←('echo'(text:'one'))('echo'(text:'two'))('echo'(text:'three'))
batchResps←h JsonRpcCl.CallBatch batchArgs
⎕←'batch results in argsVec order: ',⍕batchResps.result

⍝ --- Notification dispatch: registered handler fires, AND it's still
⍝ queued in h.Notifications either way (ADR D17: "as well as") ---
_TestHandlerLog←⍬
⎕FX'{r}←h _TestNotifyHandler notif' '#._TestHandlerLog,←⊂notif' 'r←⍬'
h JsonRpcCl.OnNotification('custom/registered' '#._TestNotifyHandler')

r←h JsonRpcCl.Call('notify'(method:'custom/registered' ⋄ notifyParams:(x:1)))
⎕←'notify(registered) ack -> ',r.result
⎕←'handler fired exactly once: ',⍕1=≢_TestHandlerLog
⎕←'handler saw method: ',(⊃_TestHandlerLog).method
⎕←'also queued in Notifications (as well as, not instead): ',⍕∨/'custom/registered'∘≡¨h.Notifications.method

⍝ A notification with no registered handler still falls through to
⍝ h.Notifications, exactly like v1 (backward compatibility).
before←≢h.Notifications
r←h JsonRpcCl.Call('notify'(method:'custom/unregistered' ⋄ notifyParams:(y:2)))
⎕←'notify(unregistered) ack -> ',r.result
⎕←'unregistered notification queued: ',⍕(≢h.Notifications)>before
⎕←'unregistered notification did NOT invoke the registered handler: ',⍕1=≢_TestHandlerLog

JsonRpcCl.Disconnect h
⎕←'done'
⎕OFF
